# Build context for the API image (Dockerfile at the repo root).
# An allowlist: everything is excluded, then only what the image needs is let back in.
# That keeps tests, docs, the console (it has its own context, web/), local virtualenvs,
# databases and any .env file out of the build context and out of the layers.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!src
!examples

# The Pi explorer worker: its manifest and lockfile (the image installs its packages itself, so a
# node_modules built on the host, for another platform, must never come in) and the worker.
!harness/pi/package.json
!harness/pi/package-lock.json
!harness/pi/worker.mjs

# Later patterns win: strip caches and local state that sit inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/.env
**/.env.*
